---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED, LEGAL, SITE_NAMES, SITE_URL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
const lang = 'en';
---
<PageLayout title={`Legal notice of ${SITE_NAMES[lang]}: publisher, host and limits`} description="Legal notice of Sole Trader Sums: the publisher Radif Partners, the host, what the UK tax estimates are for and are not, limits of liability and reuse of Crown copyright information." lang={lang} noindex={true} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Legal notice' }]} showAuthor={false}>
  <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
    <h1>Legal notice</h1>
    <p>Information given under Article 6 III-1 of French law no. 2004-575 of 21 June 2004, the publisher being established in France.</p>
    <h2>Publisher</h2>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <p>Publication director: {AUTHOR_NAME}, responsible for the content of {SITE_URL}.</p>
    <h2>Hosting provider</h2>
    <LegalIdentity mode="hosting" lang={lang} />
    <h2>Purpose of the site</h2>
    <p>The site estimates the Income Tax, National Insurance, student loan repayments, Corporation Tax and dividend tax of self-employed people and company directors in the United Kingdom for the tax year 2026/27, and explains the related deadlines, including Making Tax Digital for Income Tax. It is independent and has no link with HM Revenue and Customs, the UK Government or the Scottish Government.</p>
    <h2>Not tax advice</h2>
    <p>Results are estimates from published rates and the assumptions stated on the <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a>. They are not personal tax, legal or financial advice and do not replace the calculation HMRC makes from your return, a status determination by a client or the advice of a qualified adviser.</p>
    <h2>Liability</h2>
    <p>Each rate is read on the official page cited with it and the engine is tested, without any guarantee that no error or later change remains. The publisher cannot be held liable for a decision, a payment, a penalty or a choice of business structure based only on this site. Errors can be reported on the <a href={route('contact', lang)}>contact</a> page.</p>
    <h2>Intellectual property and reuse</h2>
    <p>Texts, graphics and code belong to the publisher. Rates and rules published on GOV.UK and legislation.gov.uk are public sector information reused under the <a href="https://www.nationalarchives.gov.uk/doc/open-government-licence/version/3/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Open Government Licence v3.0</a>, with the source named on each page.</p>
    <h2>Personal data</h2><p>The calculators run in your browser, no cookie is set and the publisher keeps no personal data; see the <a href={route('privacy', lang)}>privacy policy</a> and <a href={route('cookies', lang)}>cookies</a>.</p>
    <h2>Reporting unlawful content</h2><p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, with the page address and the reason.</p>
    <h2>Governing law</h2><p>French law. Failing an amicable solution, the courts of {LEGAL.jurisdiction} have jurisdiction, without prejudice to the mandatory rules protecting consumers in their country of residence. Updated: {LAST_UPDATED}.</p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
